  "kind": "Coding agent",
  "tagline": "Minimal, hackable coding agent: four tools and extensions for the rest.",
  "description": "Pi is a minimal, extensible agent harness for the terminal, published by Earendil and authored by Mario Zechner. pi-ai gives one API across many model providers, pi-agent-core runs the loop, and the coding agent enables read, write, edit and bash by default, with grep, find, ls, an MCP client and a QuickJS-sandboxed codemode tool built in. It does not ask for approval before tool calls and ships without sub-agents or plan mode; extensions, skills, prompt templates and Pi packages add the rest. Sessions are JSONL trees you can branch, fork and clone. Credentials come from /login (an OAuth sign-in or an API key, saved to ~/.pi/agent/auth.json), from environment variables, or from a shell command such as a secret-manager lookup.",
